      {
        "conditionKey": "a4SandKingsBoonScorchingSandshade",
        "source": "Sethos",
        "description": "A4 The Sand King's Boon: Sethos gains the Scorching Sandshade effect, increasing the DMG dealt by Shadowpiercing Shots (the burst's dusk_0-3 hits) by 700% of his Elemental Mastery. Modelled as charged_dmgIncFromEleMas_ = 7.0, which reads the scored build's OWN EM rather than the previous fixed 1400 (a 200 EM assumption that ignored the build entirely). The dusk hits carry charged_dmg_, so the ratio reaches them; ordinary Charged Attacks share that key and also receive it, which is faithful during the burst since Charged Attacks BECOME Shadowpiercing Shots. Narrower than the physical_dmgInc it replaces, which leaked onto Sethos's Normal and Plunging attacks too.",
        "states": [
          {
